diff --git a/REVISION-2.md b/REVISION-2.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5d0d042
--- /dev/null
+++ b/REVISION-2.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Revision 2: ProcessEvent startup lookup
+
+This revision addresses fragile initialization in the first compiled package.
+It checks the Object class virtual table directly before trying the actual
+default object, avoiding the inferred UClass field offset at this stage.
+It also recognizes bounded jump stubs and uses Windows function metadata to
+identify the start of the matched function. Missing or ambiguous matches still
+stop initialization instead of calling a guessed virtual-table index.
+
+The Season 27 signature remains the upstream signature. This change is a
+candidate fix for the reported startup failure, not confirmation that this
+signature matches the user's executable. Runtime verification is still needed.
+
+Close all Fortnite instances and replace both DLLs together. Keep the same
+Reboot Launcher selections described in SETUP.md.
+
+If startup stops again, press Windows+R and open `%TEMP%`. Send the files
+`Reboot-27.11-Client-startup.log` and, if present,
+`Reboot-27.11-Server-startup.log`. The new messages identify revision 2 and
+include the detected build string. The log records the candidate address,
+table lookup results, and bounded code/table details for diagnosing mismatches.
+
+The Windows workflow runs synthetic lookup tests before compiling both DLLs.
+These tests cover direct matches, jump stubs, missing objects/functions,
+ambiguous entries and inaccessible memory. They do not test Fortnite gameplay.
